  "notes": "Source chart has 10 columns because 20.8/29.5/38.3 m booms are rated in two telescoping modes (I and II). This file uses mode I columns for 12.0, 16.4, 20.8, 29.5, 38.3 and 47.0 m (12.0 and 47.0 are I,II) and mode II for 42.6 m (only mode given). Mode II gives higher values at long radii for 20.8/29.5/38.3 m (e.g. 29.5 m @26 m: mode I 2.5 t, mode II 4.0 t) - consult source for mode II. Capacities are rated lifting capacities; hook block mass (700 kg for 80 t hook, 540/500/450 kg for 60/50/35 t) and slings must be deducted (note 3 p.14). Above thick line = strength, below = stability; radii include boom deflection. Outrigger longitudinal span = 3,550 + 3,780 mm (front/rear outrigger centre to slewing centre, p.1); transverse max 7.3 m (mid 6.7/5.5 m, min 2.7 m). Operating weight and max hook height not stated numerically in datasheet. DIMS (p.1 side view): overall length 14,375 = 8,020 (boom head to front axle) + 3,950 wheelbase + 2,405; carrier length 8,455 mm -> carrier front 5,920 mm behind boom head, front axle 2.10 m, rear axle 6.05 m from carrier front; slewing centre 1,875 mm ahead of rear axle (4.175 m from carrier front); boom foot pin 2,200 mm behind slewing centre; tail swing 4,190 mm. Wheel diameter not printed (bias tyre 29.5-25), left null."
